  <refnamediv>
    <refname>cheb</refname>
    <refpurpose>Compute the Chebyshev polynomial of the first kind.</refpurpose>
  </refnamediv>


<refsynopsisdiv>
   <title>Syntax</title>
   <synopsis>
   T = cheb(n, x)
   
   </synopsis>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
   <title>Parameters</title>
   <variablelist>
        <varlistentry>
            <term>n:</term>
            <listitem><para> Non-negative integer. Order of the Chebyshev polynomial.</para></listitem>
        </varlistentry>
        <varlistentry>
            <term>x:</term>
            <listitem><para> Scalar or array. Input values.</para></listitem>
        </varlistentry>
        <varlistentry>
            <term>T:</term>
            <listitem><para> Scalar or array. Values of the Chebyshev polynomial of the first kind.</para></listitem>
        </varlistentry>
   </variablelist>
</refsection>

<refsection>
   <title>Description</title>
   <para>
This function computes the Chebyshev polynomial of the first kind of order `n` for the input values `x`. The function supports both scalar and array inputs for `x`.
   </para>
   <para>
</para>
</refsection>

<refsection>
   <title>Examples</title>
   <programlisting role="example"><![CDATA[
T = cheb(3, 0.5)

   ]]></programlisting>
</refsection>
</refentry>
